From 8aac29117e1905f1ce9ebbe03136a8f8de14af67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 12:03:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02335/11362] [outer-loop] validate v2 heuristic-guided on
 lp85; +lp85 to router ledger (9/9 LOO)

Operator: 'make v2 heuristic-guided and validate on lp85.' v2's A*-heuristic path
(already shipped) validated on lp85 from L0: bfs/cell_count/region_count all
solve+reproduce L1 in 5 actions, but lp85 L1 is NO-HEADROOM (BFS 272 exp;
cell_count 326 worse; region_count 272 ties) -> correctly routes to BFS. lp85 is a
HIGH-cell-impact (61) game that still wins with BFS due to low headroom, reinforcing
the headroom gate (cd82/sp80 pattern).

Fixed a select_best tie-break: a heuristic that merely TIES BFS no longer falsely
'wins' (BFS preferred on ties; a heuristic wins only if it STRICTLY beats BFS).
Added lp85 to the router ledger via select_and_learn -> winner=bfs. Ledger 8->9
games; leave-one-out generalization holds at 9/9 (lp85 held-out -> predicted bfs).
---
